# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` on a Windows clone hands CRLF to code written
# against LF, and the failure is never about line endings on the face of it:
# the artifact skill frontmatter parser reports a skill has no frontmatter, and
# the reference generator rewrites every file it checks as it checks it. Nothing
# here is a Windows program, so nothing here wants CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` rather than `text`, so git keeps detecting the fixtures that carry
# a lone carriage return on purpose — the composer and task-event tests among
# them — as binary, and leaves their content alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
